      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #42528.\n\nA single-token nucleus can renormalize to `0.9999999403953552`. When the verification coin equals that value, the draft is rejected and removing its mass leaves an empty residual. The CUDA target-only sampler then emits the last vocabulary token, even though it has zero target probability.\n\nUsing the issue's FlashInfer top-k/top-p reproduction (vocabulary size 248320, eight rows):\n\n| Verification coin | Before: first emitted token | After: first emitted token | Accepted drafts, before/after |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `0.5` | 1174 | 1174 | 3 / 3 |\n| `0.99999994` | 248319 (zero mass) | 1174 (nucleus token) | 0 / 0 |\n\n## Modifications\n\nRemember the last rejected candidate with positive target mass at the current tree node. Use it when residual sampling has no positive entry. Reset the remembered candidate after accepting a draft. The strict CDF comparison and acceptance bookkeeping stay unchanged.\n\nAdd regression cases for a rounded CDF equality, a coin above the rounded CDF, and siblings that exhaust the target support.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Native registered sampling file through the CUDA JIT path: 10 passed. The three new cases fail against upstream. A `<=` comparison alone changes the existing interior CDF boundary (emits token 1 instead of 3 at coin 0.25) and still emits a zero-mass token in the shortfall and sibling cases.\n- The issue's actual FlashInfer renormalization and CUDA sampling reproduction produces the table above.\n- Fixed-seed differential: acceptance indices, counts and emitted tokens match upstream on 1024 seeded rows at each of two threshold settings (2048 rows total).\n- Boundary checks pass for vector widths 1, 2 and 4 in deterministic and non-deterministic modes.\n\nRun on an NVIDIA L40S with CUDA 13.0, Python 3.12.11, Torch 2.14.1 and FlashInfer 0.7.0.post1.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nCUDA graph replay of the sampler plus draft-buffer reset, median microseconds over five batches of 100 replays:\n\n| Batch / draft width / vocabulary | Deterministic | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1024 / 4 / 64 | yes | 27.32 | 27.14 |\n| 1024 / 4 / 64 | no | 27.36 | 27.30 |\n| 8 / 4 / 248320 | yes | 125.29 | 125.34 |\n| 8 / 4 / 248320 | no | 108.94 | 109.88 |\n\nObserved medians differ by at most 0.86% in this one run per arm.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37234376892](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37234376892)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37234376832](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37234376832)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37234377008](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37234377008)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 2,
